12. Permission System
Role Hierarchy
Four built-in roles with numeric hierarchy:

Owner (4): Full control, can delete server
Admin (3): All permissions except ownership
Moderator (2): Moderate content and members
Member (1): Basic participation
Permission Types
30+ granular permissions including:

manage_server, manage_channels, manage_roles
kick_members, ban_members, mute_members
send_messages, manage_messages, pin_messages
view_channels, read_message_history
attach_files, embed_links
Voice: connect, speak, use_voice_activation
Permission Evaluation
The evaluatePermission() function follows Discord's model:

Check user-specific channel overrides (highest priority)
Check role-based channel overrides
Check server-wide role permissions
Fall back to default base role permissions
DENY always takes precedence over ALLOW when multiple roles conflict.

Custom Roles
Servers can create custom roles with:

Custom name and color
Icon (optional)
Position-based hierarchy
Granular permission overrides
